+# TasteBridge 0.3.0 — hosted Qloo decision tool
+
+Carlosjv. MIT-licensed experimental group decision tool. This hosted application replaces the former static landing experience; the original explicitly synthetic lab remains at `/lab/index.html`.
+
+## Behavior
+
+Review a public cultural preference for each of 2–6 guests, review 2–5 place search results including their addresses, and enter current host-reported prices/access facts. The tool applies budget, accessibility and veto constraints first, queries Qloo for each guest over the same feasible shortlist, then maximizes the lowest within-query midrank and breaks ties using the mean. Tied leaders remain explicitly identified. Users confirm the final proposal. No booking is performed.
+
+Qloo affinities are not satisfaction probabilities; neither cross-query raw affinity comparability nor independent verification of prices/accessibility is claimed. Missing or constant affinity evidence blocks a proposal. Entity selection tokens are authenticated and expire after an hour; fact reviews expire after 24 hours. Changing any input clears the displayed proposal.
+
+## Hosting and secrets
+
+Vinext/Cloudflare Workers with a D1 binding `DB`. `QLOO_API_KEY` is a server-only secret managed through Sites, never source code. The sole provider destination is `https://hackathon.api.qloo.com`; redirects are rejected. Requests time out after 15 seconds and responses are limited to 2 MB. The durable `qloo_meter` table enforces 60 total provider calls for this demo revision across restarts/concurrent requests. This is an application limit, not a claim about the provider's quota. No automatic refill or retry. Search and affinity responses are cached for one hour; records contain public cultural entity data, not user names. Hosting does not use a model API.
+
+## Development
+
+Install dependencies using the supported Sites helper; run `node test-policy.mjs` and `node test-api-local.mjs` for decision/constraint checks. Generate D1 migrations with `npm run db:generate`. Build through the Sites build helper. Both schema and generated SQL are versioned. GET `/api/taste` describes the bounded tool interface; POST accepts `search` and `evaluate`. Same-origin required. This is a deterministic agentic decision tool, not a claim that a deployed autonomous LLM agent has been tested.
+
+## Verification limits
+
+Build and pure decision-policy tests pass. The original Python adapter authenticated against Qloo. A real cross-domain Insights request returned incomplete evidence and correctly caused abstention. Browser UI visual QA is unavailable in this execution environment. Public URL readiness and live hosted calls must be verified after deployment. The upstream public GitHub repository describes the earlier Python runtime until synchronized; do not claim this source revision is already published there.
+
+## Availability and policy audit — 0.3.2
+
+The home page now includes an interactive **recorded Qloo evidence** replay from the verified 19 October run. It requires no new provider call and is explicitly distinguished from live search. The two test profiles disagree; recomputation returns a tie. Applying a veto leaves insufficient options and causes abstention. This preserves a usable, honest evidence walkthrough if the live allowance is exhausted; it does not remove the live quota limitation or substitute for the live demo requirement.
+
+`node benchmark-policy.mjs` exhaustively enumerates 216 synthetic strict ordinal profiles for three guests and three options. Against a mean-only midrank baseline, max-min changes the choice in 27 cases (12.5%), improves the minimum in those 27, and leaves it equal in 189. Average minimum-rank gain is 0.0625, while average mean-rank sacrifice is 0.013889 (maximum 1/6). These are designed-policy properties on synthetic preferences, not a Qloo/LLM accuracy comparison or evidence of real user satisfaction. Results are at `/evidence/synthetic-policy-benchmark.json`.
+
+POST request bodies are now bounded while streaming, before parsing, at 192,000 bytes. API metadata reports the remaining live allowance. The recorded replay is never substituted silently for a live query.
+
+Local audit correction: a constant first guest affinity now abstains immediately before additional provider requests. The API regression harness mocks fetch and D1 and does not validate the deployment.
+
+
+## Current public source distribution — 26 October 2026
+
+The demo now links to `/source/index.html`, which serves a complete source ZIP and per-file SHA-256 manifest. The source includes actionable recovery when fewer than two places meet the entered constraints, preserving budget/access/vetoes. The live UI and recorded example share this recovery presentation.
+
+The source archive excludes only installed dependencies, build products, secrets/runtime data and its own generated archive/manifest. Rebuild it with `python3 scripts/export_public_source.py` in a Git checkout. For local checks, use Node 24 and run `node test-policy.mjs`, `node test-rank-stability.mjs`, `node test-recovery.mjs`, and `node test-api-local.mjs`. These checks require no API key and do not make live provider requests.
+
+The recovery release passed its production build, 11 new recovery checks, four mocked route recovery cases, 864 separately reviewed constraint combinations and four rendered component cases. The published recovery UI and tie were checked in a browser. No new live Qloo request was used. These are software-correctness checks, not customer satisfaction or competition superiority. Earlier dated readiness statements above are historical.
+
+The historical public GitHub repository is preserved, but its current integration rejects write access. This hosting therefore distributes the current application source directly; the GitHub repository is not claimed to be synchronized.
+
+## Input validation and search-state correction — 26 October 2026
+
+An explicitly supplied `veto` must now be a JSON boolean. Missing `veto` preserves the existing `false` default. Malformed values are rejected before entity-proof verification, database access or provider requests. The host already controls this fact; this correction improves input validation and does not establish a bypass of another user's authorization.
+
+Editing a search query or category now clears its previous results and error. Responses from an older search cannot replace the current search state, including after a confirmed selection. This corrects stale feedback and selection state; no cross-site scripting or privilege escalation was demonstrated.
+
+Run `node test-security-validation.mjs` and `node test-search-revision.mjs` for the focused regressions. They execute the real source with mocked platform/provider or React hook behavior, respectively, and make no live provider calls. The same expectations yield 5/22 and 2/12 passing checks on the prior source, and 22/22 and 12/12 after the correction. These results measure these specific fixes, not general security coverage. Live HTTP checks separately confirmed rejection of absent/foreign origins and an invalid entity proof. A real browser reproduced the stale-error behavior before this update; publication and subsequent verification are recorded in the deployment report.
+
+## Guest identity correction — 27 October 2026
+
+Removing a guest now preserves each remaining guest's search, category and selected preference. Guest cards use stable, non-recycled identities, and selection callbacks target that identity instead of a changing row position. This also prevents a delayed selection for a removed guest from changing another guest.
+
+The defect was reproduced in the published browser UI without provider calls: after entering Arrival, Spirited Away and The Matrix in three guest search fields, removing the first guest incorrectly kept Arrival and Spirited Away. The required result is Spirited Away and The Matrix.
+
+Run `node test-guest-identity.mjs` for six focused regression checks. The test evaluates the actual Home JSX and event callbacks using the real JSX runtime and deterministic hooks; it does not emulate the React reconciler or claim browser coverage. The unchanged assertions pass 2/6 on the prior release and 6/6 after this correction. Separate browser verification belongs to the release report. No ranking policy, provider quota or API contract was changed.
+
+## Live readiness and source refresh — 30 October 2026
+
+A new panel before the live form reads server configuration and the existing shared allowance without contacting Qloo or reserving calls. It distinguishes an unconfigured demo, unknown allowance, exhausted allowance and a positive remaining count, and links to the dated recorded example. It refreshes on mount or explicit request with a five-second timeout and no automatic retry. Configuration presence does not verify key validity, expiry or provider health. Search, evaluation, ranking, the 60-call cap and one-hour cache are unchanged.
+
+The readiness route/message checks passed 22 expectations and the component harness passed eight. A real React server render, production build and browser hydration/refresh were checked without provider calls. A 390-pixel frame layout check found no horizontal overflow; this does not establish full mobile usability. Earlier dated readiness notes above describe their historical executions.
+
+The public source exporter now uses deterministic metadata and supports `python3 scripts/export_public_source.py --verify`. The manifest identifies the exact included bytes and modes without asserting deployment or repository synchronization. The public repository's newest delivery manifest is the separate record of its source commit.
+
+Judging access remains bounded by the shared allowance and provider credential availability. The Qloo rules require free unrestricted testing through the judging period. This readiness panel does not resolve or certify compliance with that requirement; no allowance was reset or expanded.
