+<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>TasteBridge · A plan with room for everyone</title><meta name="description" content="An interactive synthetic-data lab for more balanced group cultural choices."><link rel="stylesheet" href="style.css"></head><body>
+<header><a class="brand" href="./">Taste<span>Bridge</span><i>↗</i></a><span class="badge">PROTOTYPE / 01</span></header>
+<main><section class="intro"><p class="eyebrow">GROUP CULTURE, CONSIDERED</p><h1>A shared plan.<br><em>Room for everyone.</em></h1><p class="lede">See what changes when the quietest preference matters as much as the loudest. Explore a group decision before asking anyone to agree.</p></section>
+<aside class="notice"><strong>Synthetic decision lab</strong><span>All venues, prices, access facts and scores below are invented. Qloo is not connected. This is a decision prototype, not a live recommendation or booking service.</span></aside>
+<div class="workspace"><section class="controls"><div class="section-title"><span class="step">01</span><h2>Set the scene</h2></div><label for="scenario">Starting scenario</label><select id="scenario"><option value="conflict">Two agree. One gets left behind.</option><option value="aligned">Everyone is on the same wavelength.</option><option value="missing">One guest's evidence is missing.</option></select><label for="budget">Budget per guest (€)</label><input id="budget" type="number" min="0" max="1000" value="25"><label class="check"><input id="access" type="checkbox" checked> Require confirmed step-free access</label><p class="hint">Taste cannot establish accessibility. Unknown access is held for clarification when this requirement is on.</p><button id="reset" class="secondary">Reset scenario</button><div class="legend"><span>A · Guest A</span><span>B · Guest B</span><span>C · Guest C</span></div><p class="hint">Scores are hypothetical preference proxies, not probabilities. Adjust them to challenge the decision.</p></section>
+<section><div class="section-title"><span class="step">02</span><h2>Explore the options</h2></div><div id="candidates"></div></section></div>
+<section class="decision" aria-live="polite"><div class="section-title"><span class="step">03</span><h2>The group proposal</h2></div><div id="result"></div><div class="actions"><button id="confirm">Confirm this proposal</button><button id="export" class="secondary">Download decision JSON</button></div><p id="confirmation" role="status"></p></section>
+<section class="method"><h2>What the rule values</h2><p>First respect vetoes, budget and required facts. Then choose the highest minimum preference score; break ties with the group average. This prioritizes the weakest match and can lower the average. It is a transparent choice, not proof of the best experience.</p><p><strong>Next validation:</strong> Qloo integration, comparable affinity evidence, real venue facts and host pilots. No customer outcome, revenue or award is claimed.</p></section></main><footer>CARLOSJV · TASTEBRIDGE <span>Designed for a conversation, not an automatic booking.</span></footer><script type="module" src="app.mjs"></script></body></html>
