+<a href="/">← TasteBridge demo</a><h1>Read and reproduce TasteBridge</h1>
+<p>Application source snapshot for this demo. Includes the shared live-allowance display, stable guest identities, strict veto validation, search-state correction, constraint recovery, the recorded example, local tests, locked dependencies, build integration and this download page.</p>
+<ul><li><a href="TasteBridge-source.zip" download>Download the complete application source ZIP</a></li><li><a href="source-manifest.json">SHA-256 checksums and exact source inventory</a></li><li><a href="https://github.com/carlosjunquerovila-afk/tastebridge" rel="noreferrer">Public repository, source delivery and release history</a></li></ul>
+<p>The ZIP contains the application source and MIT license, including retained third-party notices. It excludes installed dependencies, build output, credentials, runtime data and the generated ZIP and manifest themselves. After extracting, read <code>README.md</code>. The included <code>scripts/export_public_source.py</code> documents how this distribution is built.</p>
+<p>Use Node 24 and Python 3. The local policy, rank, recovery and mocked-route tests require no API key or provider calls. Building needs the locked dependencies and the included Sites integration. Running a separate live instance needs your own Qloo key and D1 setup; the public demo requires no key from visitors.</p>
